A seek the source turns down fails, says why, and leaves things as they were

Three things that together made a film end when the request a seek made
was refused, as it is when a token has run out an hour into the film.

matroska: a seek looks the place up in the index and goes to its bytes.
Whether the bytes could be gone to was not looked at. The connection
stayed where it was and the demuxer went on as if it stood at the
cluster it had asked for. The seek now fails, and the generic seek that
is tried next returns what the connection said.

http: the answer that refuses a request has a length of its own, zero as
a rule, and that was kept as the length of the file. Every seek after it
lay "past the end", was granted without a request being made, and the
next read was the end of the file. The length is put back with the rest
of what a failed seek puts back.

http: a 401 to a request for a part of a file was reported as an
"unexpected offset", an input/output error, because the answer names no
part. It is reported as the status it is.

--- a/libavformat/http.c	2026-11-14 02:22:14
+++ b/libavformat/http.c	2026-11-14 02:22:14
@@ -1738,7 +1738,9 @@
     if (s->new_location)
         s->off = off;
 
-    if (off != s->off) {
+    /* A request that was turned down for want of credentials has no
+     * offset to compare. The caller looks at the status, and says that. */
+    if (off != s->off && s->http_code != 401 && s->http_code != 407) {
         av_log(h, AV_LOG_ERROR,
                "Unexpected offset: expected %"PRIu64", got %"PRIu64"\n",
                off, s->off);
@@ -2140,6 +2142,7 @@
     HTTPContext *s = h->priv_data;
     URLContext *old_hd = NULL;
     uint64_t old_off = s->off;
+    uint64_t old_filesize = s->filesize;
     uint8_t old_buf[BUFFER_SIZE];
     int old_buf_size, ret;
     AVDictionary *options = NULL;
@@ -2231,6 +2234,9 @@
             s->hd      = old_hd;
             s->off     = old_off;
         }
+        /* The answer that turned the request down had a length of its
+         * own, which is not the file's. */
+        s->filesize = old_filesize;
         av_dict_free(&options);
         return ret;
     }
--- a/libavformat/matroskadec.c	2026-11-14 02:14:38
+++ b/libavformat/matroskadec.c	2026-11-14 02:14:38
@@ -4540,7 +4540,12 @@
     }
 
     /* We seek to a level 1 element, so set the appropriate status. */
-    matroska_reset_status(matroska, 0, sti->index_entries[index].pos);
+    if (matroska_reset_status(matroska, 0, sti->index_entries[index].pos) < 0) {
+        /* The bytes of that place could not be had, and the reader stands
+         * where it stood. Saying the seek went through would have what
+         * comes next read as if it were the cluster that was asked for. */
+        goto err;
+    }
     if (flags & AVSEEK_FLAG_ANY) {
         sti->skip_to_keyframe = 0;
         matroska->skip_to_timecode = timestamp;
